WEBVTT

00:37.415 --> 00:39.788
Yesterday...

00:39.788 --> 00:40.953
Yesterday?

00:40.953 --> 00:42.412
We kissed.

00:42.412 --> 00:43.465
What?

00:43.465 --> 00:46.453
I was so jittery about seeing you again
that sleep completely escaped me.

00:46.453 --> 00:49.566
Did you manage to get any rest?

00:51.771 --> 00:53.628
Ui Yeong, is it true?

00:53.628 --> 00:56.568
Did you kiss?

00:56.568 --> 00:57.698
Yeah, we did.

00:57.698 --> 01:02.169
But... Do I really have to admit that publicly?

01:02.169 --> 01:03.746
Are you going to stay here?

01:03.746 --> 01:07.352
We have something important to discuss.

01:17.739 --> 01:22.205
[Episode 5]

01:22.958 --> 01:25.236
What's so important?

01:25.236 --> 01:27.438
Wait...

01:28.371 --> 01:30.135
We may have missed each other before,

01:30.135 --> 01:32.345
but we ended up meeting again.

01:32.345 --> 01:34.762
- And we kissed.
- Once I decide something isn't right,

01:34.762 --> 01:36.786
- The way he's wrapping this up...
- I don't go back on it.

01:36.786 --> 01:38.264
sounds exactly like a confession.

01:38.264 --> 01:39.484
What should we do?

01:39.484 --> 01:43.390
Should we just start dating
and see how it goes?

01:43.390 --> 01:45.293
Ms. Ui Yeong?

01:45.293 --> 01:48.179
I meant we should work together.

01:48.179 --> 01:52.358
Oh, what did you say?

01:53.112 --> 01:57.658
Eun Ho brought this yesterday
when he dropped off the luggage.

01:58.696 --> 02:02.653
Sua's really good at drawing.

02:02.653 --> 02:04.124
But why...

02:04.124 --> 02:08.070
Oh, she drew on it.

02:15.656 --> 02:17.833
It sounded like a losing deal for the hotel.

02:17.833 --> 02:20.097
They even agreed to run the pop-up

02:20.097 --> 02:22.418
within the concept and budget we proposed.

02:22.418 --> 02:24.109
And I liked their new idea even more,

02:24.109 --> 02:26.507
[Deluxe Double Room & Signature Furniture]
creating package rooms featuring the furniture.

02:26.507 --> 02:29.044
This way,
guests can naturally try out the furniture.

02:29.044 --> 02:32.590
For furniture makers,
it is not about how pretty it looks.

02:32.590 --> 02:35.444
We always want people to know
how sturdy it really is.

02:35.444 --> 02:37.616
I see.

02:38.717 --> 02:40.355
About that day,

02:40.355 --> 02:43.013
I'm sorry I got angry

02:43.013 --> 02:44.704
without even hearing you out.

02:44.704 --> 02:45.829
You don't have to apologize.

02:45.829 --> 02:49.403
I'm really grateful that you changed your mind.

02:49.403 --> 02:52.389
Let's work well together from now on.

02:52.389 --> 02:53.434
- Okay.
- Then,

02:53.434 --> 02:55.379
let's get the concept approved by the brand

02:55.379 --> 02:57.279
and move straight into the kickoff meeting.

02:57.279 --> 03:00.820
How does your schedule look?
The sooner the better for us.

03:00.820 --> 03:02.650
Should we check our schedules?

03:02.650 --> 03:04.963
Sounds good.

03:06.598 --> 03:09.172
We're ready anytime.

03:09.172 --> 03:11.161
Maybe Monday?

03:12.994 --> 03:14.731
Alright then, take care.

03:14.731 --> 03:17.533
Ms. Ui Yeong, well...

03:18.434 --> 03:20.926
The ki...

03:20.926 --> 03:22.476
The ki...

03:22.476 --> 03:24.048
Key?

03:24.048 --> 03:25.513
Keyring, no.

03:25.513 --> 03:27.916
Cream. There's cream on your face, right here.

03:29.465 --> 03:31.948
Maybe from the latte?

03:31.948 --> 03:34.402
Actually, I mean...

03:34.402 --> 03:36.189
The...

03:36.189 --> 03:38.772
K-Key...

03:38.772 --> 03:40.795
Oh, here it is.

03:42.459 --> 03:45.036
Oh, okay.

03:46.582 --> 03:48.259
Alright then, I'll get going.

03:48.259 --> 03:50.602
Bye.

03:55.501 --> 03:59.367
But I had a latte.
Why is there cream on my face?

03:59.999 --> 04:02.232
Come to think of it...

04:02.232 --> 04:06.452
Is that really how the kiss thing ended?

04:09.216 --> 04:11.392
I don't know.

04:17.836 --> 04:20.668
What on earth did I just say?

04:22.322 --> 04:25.382
They kissed?

04:28.534 --> 04:31.933
The wood is pretty sensitive.

04:31.933 --> 04:33.670
Depending on the temperature and humidity,

04:33.670 --> 04:36.494
it expands and contracts.

04:36.494 --> 04:40.980
So sometimes the furniture can warp a little.

04:42.761 --> 04:44.405
- Why?
- Sorry?

04:44.405 --> 04:45.448
- What?
- What?

04:45.448 --> 04:46.669
- Oh.
- What do you mean?

04:46.669 --> 04:48.073
Oh, what I mean is

04:48.073 --> 04:50.683
we offer free repairs for a year.

04:50.683 --> 04:53.146
Yeah, that's it.

04:53.146 --> 04:55.707
Right.

04:55.707 --> 04:58.759
[After work, let's go to your place.]

05:00.773 --> 05:03.810
So you really don't need to worry about that.

05:03.810 --> 05:06.456
Please take your time and have a look around.

05:13.426 --> 05:15.882
You've got some nerve, man.

05:15.882 --> 05:17.741
I bet everyone in heaven knows by now.

05:17.741 --> 05:19.841
How do you kiss someone in a church?

05:19.841 --> 05:21.806
I wasn't thinking. I swear.

05:21.806 --> 05:26.022
About the kiss, or telling everyone about it.

05:26.022 --> 05:28.680
I did it because I wasn't thinking.

05:28.680 --> 05:30.024
You did well.

05:30.024 --> 05:31.170
Hey.

05:31.170 --> 05:33.847
There's no stamp stronger than a kiss.

05:33.847 --> 05:35.397
You've stamped it already,

05:35.397 --> 05:37.150
so don't even think about backing out.

05:37.150 --> 05:38.454
- Uncle.
- Take responsibility...

05:38.454 --> 05:39.628
Dad.

05:39.628 --> 05:41.707
What? You were listening?

05:41.707 --> 05:44.856
Those don't have noise-canceling, remember?

05:45.989 --> 05:47.274
Sua,

05:47.274 --> 05:49.266
listen.

05:49.266 --> 05:51.914
Your uncle here kissed someone.

05:51.914 --> 05:53.988
Like when you give your dad a peck.

05:55.703 --> 05:58.477
So are you two in a relationship now?

05:58.477 --> 06:00.301
- Right.
- But you know,

06:00.301 --> 06:03.261
that idea is totally outdated, huh?

06:03.261 --> 06:05.325
What responsibility is there from a kiss?

06:05.325 --> 06:07.529
Did anyone get hurt? Did something break?

06:07.529 --> 06:09.049
Well...

06:09.049 --> 06:11.283
I think your uncle might be a little broken.

06:11.283 --> 06:14.243
Not broken. Just softer.

06:14.243 --> 06:17.287
That's what happens when you like someone.

06:17.287 --> 06:19.524
Yeah, you're right.

06:19.524 --> 06:21.061
It's been so long I forgot.

06:21.061 --> 06:22.144
Congrats, Uncle.

06:22.144 --> 06:25.781
Liking someone is something to celebrate.

06:25.781 --> 06:28.687
So what are you going to do?

06:29.488 --> 06:33.464
I should tell her I'll work hard
and do dating properly this time.

06:33.464 --> 06:34.768
You got this.

06:34.768 --> 06:36.488
Tell me if something good happens.

06:36.488 --> 06:38.458
And tell me if you need cheering up too.

06:38.458 --> 06:42.037
You know we're always on your side.

06:51.763 --> 06:53.954
Hey, Lee Sua.

06:53.954 --> 06:55.906
How do you know all this stuff?

06:55.906 --> 06:59.247
Have you dated before?

06:59.247 --> 07:01.456
You said those don't have noise canceling, huh?

07:01.456 --> 07:05.643
Hey, you need my permission to date, okay?

07:05.643 --> 07:08.856
But I'm not giving permission...

07:08.856 --> 07:11.503
You're not dating anyone, right?

07:37.318 --> 07:39.285
This is our division head.

07:39.285 --> 07:41.075
And these are the representatives from HOME.

07:41.075 --> 07:44.035
I'm Song Tae Seop.

07:44.035 --> 07:46.635
I'm Lee Eun Ho.

07:51.365 --> 07:53.772
We're ready.

07:54.425 --> 07:56.229
Hello.

07:56.229 --> 07:58.562
- Hello.
- Nice to meet you.

07:58.562 --> 08:00.362
Sir...

08:04.072 --> 08:06.642
Attorney Kang, it's been a while.

08:06.642 --> 08:08.122
Hello.

08:08.122 --> 08:11.832
I heard there was an unpleasant incident
during the bidding process.

08:11.832 --> 08:14.222
Thank you for accepting the proposal again.

08:14.222 --> 08:15.986
We've already received a sufficient apology.

08:15.986 --> 08:19.012
From here on, I hope both companies
can work together on this project.

08:19.012 --> 08:21.732
We don't hold grudges.

08:24.251 --> 08:26.275
So, this is the pop-up concept.

08:26.275 --> 08:28.853
It draws inspiration from a local bar

08:28.853 --> 08:30.996
that captures the heritage of Deerfiddich,

08:30.996 --> 08:32.599
a whiskey that has delivered

08:32.599 --> 08:34.773
the same signature sip for over a century...

08:34.773 --> 08:36.673
After passing through
a photo zone and mini bar...

08:36.673 --> 08:38.643
Showcasing the history of Deerfiddich...

08:38.643 --> 08:40.260
Allowing them to experience the whiskey

08:40.260 --> 08:43.423
in a more sensory way.

08:48.182 --> 08:50.119
In the second exhibition zone,

08:50.119 --> 08:52.926
the actual bottles will be displayed
by aging year,

08:52.926 --> 08:57.771
with explanations of
each one's character and appeal.

08:57.771 --> 08:59.795
I'm looking forward to the results.

08:59.795 --> 09:02.106
Please support whatever HOME needs.

09:02.106 --> 09:02.877
- Yes.
- Got it.

09:02.877 --> 09:05.485
Thank you.

09:05.485 --> 09:07.723
Thank you.

09:11.509 --> 09:12.653
So...

09:12.653 --> 09:14.956
I told them to take extra care preparing this.

09:14.956 --> 09:15.987
How is it?

09:15.987 --> 09:18.136
- It's really good.
- That's a relief.

09:18.136 --> 09:19.542
Please enjoy.

09:19.542 --> 09:20.706
By the way,

09:20.706 --> 09:24.063
what made you change your mind?

09:25.806 --> 09:28.433
Because of Ms. Ui Yeong.

09:31.900 --> 09:33.075
Oh, well...

09:33.075 --> 09:36.115
He tends to keep things short,
so people sometimes misunderstand him.

09:36.115 --> 09:38.932
What he means is
Ms. Ui Yeong's passion changed our minds.

09:38.932 --> 09:41.618
That's what he meant.

09:41.618 --> 09:46.498
I've never seen anyone fold animals
out of towels that well before.

09:46.498 --> 09:49.448
She really does handle things
with a lot of creativity.

09:49.448 --> 09:50.502
Yes, she really does.

09:50.502 --> 09:53.313
So going forward,
I'd like to keep communicating

09:53.313 --> 09:56.213
through Ms. Ui Yeong as well.

09:56.213 --> 09:57.436
Yes, that sounds good.

09:57.436 --> 09:59.883
I'll be the one coordinating with the brand,

09:59.883 --> 10:02.354
so just keep me updated on the progress.

10:02.354 --> 10:03.681
Okay.

10:03.681 --> 10:07.471
Then if you need anything,
please feel free to contact me anytime.

10:07.471 --> 10:09.416
Sure.

10:09.416 --> 10:12.216
Please, go ahead and eat.

10:14.861 --> 10:16.277
We have to work on the pop-up booth

10:16.277 --> 10:18.808
and the hotel room furniture at the same time,

10:18.808 --> 10:21.591
so I'm a little worried
the schedule might be tight.

10:21.591 --> 10:22.861
Yeah, that's true.

10:22.861 --> 10:25.381
We'll probably be busy for a while,

10:25.381 --> 10:27.965
so how about we go on dates after work?

10:27.965 --> 10:30.035
"Dates?"

10:32.045 --> 10:34.698
- You know we're at work, right?
- Oh, right.

10:36.038 --> 10:39.972
Good thing no one else heard that.

10:39.972 --> 10:42.651
So, want to?

10:43.350 --> 10:45.677
Yeah, I'd like that.

10:51.538 --> 10:54.935
Hold it together.
Even if you miss him, hold it in.

10:54.935 --> 10:56.279
You're getting butterflies again?

10:56.279 --> 10:58.749
You look totally obsessed.

10:58.749 --> 11:00.161
What?

11:00.161 --> 11:01.739
Look at this.

11:01.739 --> 11:03.245
[You're getting butterflies in your celery]
This is pretty fun.

11:03.245 --> 11:05.356
[You look totally obsessed with melon]

11:05.356 --> 11:08.474
[Even if you miss grapes, hold it in]
[Hold these cherries]

11:08.474 --> 11:11.258
Should we grab a coffee
before heading back to the office?

11:11.258 --> 11:13.638
Sounds good.

11:16.010 --> 11:17.589
Those spicy chicken feet we had...

11:17.589 --> 11:19.451
I keep thinking about them.

11:19.451 --> 11:21.362
At first I was like,

11:21.362 --> 11:24.354
how do you even eat that?

11:24.354 --> 11:26.378
They're not really used overseas, right?

11:26.378 --> 11:29.854
But once you get hooked on that spicy flavor,
there's no going back.

11:29.854 --> 11:32.113
Take me there again next time. To Eat Eat Club.

11:32.113 --> 11:34.492
Sure.

11:34.492 --> 11:36.117
I should get going.

11:36.117 --> 11:39.007
I'm going to grab some coffee for the team.
Go on ahead.

11:39.007 --> 11:42.453
- Thanks for today.
- No problem.

11:50.206 --> 11:51.490
- Yes, Ui Yeong.
- Hyun Min,

11:51.490 --> 11:53.321
I'm about to grab a coffee
before I head back to the office.

11:53.321 --> 11:54.687
What do you and Sae Byeok want?

11:54.687 --> 11:57.158
Then... two iced Americanos, please.

11:57.158 --> 11:59.336
Oh, and sandwiches too.

11:59.336 --> 12:01.492
What? You haven't eaten yet?

12:01.492 --> 12:03.196
Not me. Sae Byeok.

12:03.196 --> 12:06.256
Skipping meals won't help with mistakes anyway.

12:06.256 --> 12:07.680
Oh really?

12:07.680 --> 12:10.836
Alright, got it.

12:26.611 --> 12:28.608
Are you just getting to work?

12:28.608 --> 12:31.776
Yeah. Monday through Wednesday,
I work from six to closing.

12:31.776 --> 12:34.705
Thursday and Friday, from one to six.

12:34.705 --> 12:35.917
So what,

12:35.917 --> 12:38.127
you ended up working
with that guy from the blind date?

12:38.127 --> 12:41.893
Turns out he's involved in the bid
our team submitted.

12:41.893 --> 12:44.093
Isn't that crazy?

12:46.094 --> 12:48.030
That's crazy.

12:48.030 --> 12:50.890
So, are you two dating now?

12:52.288 --> 12:53.387
No.

12:53.387 --> 12:55.680
Not that far.

12:56.340 --> 12:57.379
Right.

12:57.379 --> 12:58.439
You're not twenty anymore.

12:58.439 --> 13:01.082
You can't give your whole heart over one kiss.

13:01.082 --> 13:03.252
I've kissed a lot in my life.

13:03.252 --> 13:06.620
If you count acting too,
probably five hundred times.

13:06.620 --> 13:11.182
Once you start attaching meaning to it,
things just get complicated.

13:11.182 --> 13:14.208
I could even kiss someone
right now if I wanted.

13:15.315 --> 13:18.082
What are you doing?

13:19.762 --> 13:22.726
And sure, a kiss isn't everything,

13:22.726 --> 13:26.259
but it's not nothing either.

13:26.259 --> 13:28.079
Seriously, how have you been living?

13:28.079 --> 13:31.052
Just normally.

13:35.307 --> 13:39.851
So how does it feel riding something like that?

13:39.851 --> 13:43.702
Like you're cutting through the air.

13:43.702 --> 13:44.777
"Cutting?"

13:44.777 --> 13:46.801
If you're curious,
want me to take you for a ride?

13:46.801 --> 13:48.398
Yeah, sure.

13:48.398 --> 13:50.571
Next time.

13:51.700 --> 13:54.986
[Break Room]

14:08.107 --> 14:11.137
Sae Byeok, your internship ends soon, right?

14:11.137 --> 14:13.201
I happened to see it
while organizing the contracts.

14:13.201 --> 14:15.727
Yes. It ends in about a month.

14:15.727 --> 14:18.137
Honestly, hotels may look glamorous,

14:18.137 --> 14:22.161
but the pay isn't great
compared to the workload.

14:22.161 --> 14:24.511
Your starting salary matters a lot.

14:24.511 --> 14:27.011
I have a close junior who works at a bank.

14:27.011 --> 14:29.561
If I ask, he could give you some advice.

14:29.561 --> 14:32.275
Maybe the three of us could meet sometime...

14:32.275 --> 14:35.201
I'll figure it out myself.

14:35.201 --> 14:36.942
Okay.

14:36.942 --> 14:38.772
Where are you? I need to whip you into shape.

14:38.772 --> 14:39.832
Get to the conference room.

14:39.832 --> 14:42.835
Ms. Ui Yeong is looking for me,

14:42.835 --> 14:46.015
- so I'll head over first.
- Sure.

14:53.604 --> 14:56.227
Are you on a diet these days?

14:56.227 --> 14:58.797
No, I'm not.

14:58.797 --> 15:01.434
Then work must be so hard you can't even eat.

15:01.434 --> 15:04.418
It's okay. Sometimes work really is that tough.

15:04.418 --> 15:06.375
But you learned something big this time.

15:06.375 --> 15:09.415
You must've been really disappointed in me.

15:09.415 --> 15:11.352
Disappointed over one mistake? Come on.

15:11.352 --> 15:12.645
Then it's time you learn

15:12.645 --> 15:17.801
how much strength a meal gives you,
even when things are tough.

15:17.801 --> 15:19.625
Thank you.

15:19.625 --> 15:22.062
Eat this and get your energy back.
Then help me out.

15:22.062 --> 15:23.726
- Yeah?
- I'd like you...

15:23.726 --> 15:26.092
to handle the backup work
for this pop-up project.

15:26.092 --> 15:28.471
Me?

15:28.471 --> 15:30.669
But if I do it...

15:30.669 --> 15:32.282
won't HOME hate that idea?

15:32.282 --> 15:33.302
If it were me,

15:33.302 --> 15:35.599
I'd dislike someone who runs away
after making a mistake.

15:35.599 --> 15:36.806
But someone who takes responsibility
and tries to fix it

15:36.806 --> 15:39.792
is someone I'd want to work with again.

15:39.792 --> 15:41.263
Ui Yeong...

15:41.263 --> 15:43.089
You're going to see it through, right?

15:43.089 --> 15:46.709
Yes! I'll do it.

15:46.709 --> 15:49.675
Alright, who's up first?

16:02.604 --> 16:03.677
I'll keep it short.

16:03.677 --> 16:04.834
When people stay at a hotel,

16:04.834 --> 16:07.128
how many actually unpack
and organize their things in the cabinet?

16:07.128 --> 16:09.630
- Think again. Make it more practical.
- Yes, sir.

16:09.630 --> 16:11.961
And you two need to check the floor plan again.

16:11.961 --> 16:13.487
Where do you expect to fit furniture this big?

16:13.487 --> 16:15.704
Even after staring at it with barely any sleep,

16:15.704 --> 16:18.345
the room's still small
and the furniture fills it up.

16:18.345 --> 16:20.555
Sir, this floor plan is like a blank canvas

16:20.555 --> 16:23.815
with nowhere left to add anything.

16:25.849 --> 16:28.012
I know it's not an easy job.

16:28.012 --> 16:29.642
Let's call it a day.

16:29.642 --> 16:31.403
Head home early and get some rest.

16:31.403 --> 16:33.969
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

17:01.558 --> 17:04.155
This is so heavy.

17:04.155 --> 17:07.861
I'm telling you, it's cheapest online.

17:07.861 --> 17:10.018
Just search it, sort by minimum order,

17:10.018 --> 17:12.108
and it gets delivered
to your door the next day.

17:12.108 --> 17:14.498
I feel better seeing things in person.

17:14.498 --> 17:16.739
I can check the expiration dates myself

17:16.739 --> 17:19.560
and catch up with a friend while I'm at it.

17:19.560 --> 17:21.291
And make your friend carry your stuff too?

17:21.291 --> 17:24.924
Much appreciated, my friend.

17:24.924 --> 17:25.957
So?

17:25.957 --> 17:28.242
What's it like working
with that guy from the blind date?

17:28.242 --> 17:29.960
Oh, that?

17:29.960 --> 17:32.346
We just... work.

17:32.346 --> 17:34.470
I mean, I want to text him first sometimes,

17:34.470 --> 17:37.010
but I know he's busy, so it feels weird.

17:37.010 --> 17:39.734
Wouldn't it be nice if he texted me first?

17:39.734 --> 17:43.053
- After we kissed...
- Wait, what?

17:43.053 --> 17:45.011
You kissed that guy?

17:45.011 --> 17:47.761
When?

17:47.761 --> 17:50.160
Oh, that was before...

17:50.160 --> 17:52.757
The mood just suddenly got kind of...

17:52.757 --> 17:54.981
soft and romantic.

17:54.981 --> 17:57.660
Are you going to nag me about it?

17:58.767 --> 18:01.145
No, who am I to do that?

18:01.145 --> 18:02.463
I mean, even I...

18:02.463 --> 18:04.476
With someone I met through a used item deal...

18:04.476 --> 18:05.846
What?

18:05.846 --> 18:08.280
Never mind. Stuff like that happens.

18:08.280 --> 18:09.567
Ui Yeong, want to work out?

18:09.567 --> 18:12.996
I literally just worked out. I'm exhausted.

18:12.996 --> 18:14.743
I'll take my pay and go.

18:14.743 --> 18:16.233
- Bye.
- Get home safe.

18:16.233 --> 18:18.713
Thanks.

18:24.229 --> 18:26.899
Ms. Ui Yeong, do you have time tomorrow?

18:26.899 --> 18:28.395
Huh?

18:28.395 --> 18:30.595
He texted?

18:39.169 --> 18:42.202
A peck must be nice.

18:42.202 --> 18:45.795
A peck turns into a kiss,

18:45.795 --> 18:47.855
and when you kiss...

18:48.916 --> 18:53.742
It's not easy for two people
to have that kind of chemistry right away.

19:06.536 --> 19:09.755
I've got work, so I'll head out first.

19:18.378 --> 19:20.911
I've never had a Cinderella-at-night moment

19:20.911 --> 19:23.858
like that before.

19:24.528 --> 19:28.122
- Cinderella?
- No idea.

19:36.074 --> 19:37.580
- Ma'am.
- Yes?

19:37.580 --> 19:39.144
Do you have a moment?

19:39.144 --> 19:42.784
[Deukgeun Deukgeun Gym]
Seven, eight, nine, ten.

19:45.125 --> 19:47.203
So today is your last PT session.

19:47.203 --> 19:49.580
You can feel the difference, right?

19:49.580 --> 19:51.773
Maybe... I lost one or two kilos.

19:51.773 --> 19:55.220
It's about the same as after
one trip to the bathroom.

19:55.220 --> 19:58.216
But you've gained muscle and lost body fat.

19:58.216 --> 20:00.240
If the scale changed by one or two kilos,

20:00.240 --> 20:02.043
that's actually great progress.

20:02.043 --> 20:04.177
You've built a solid workout habit.

20:04.177 --> 20:07.407
But the money leaving my account
is very noticeable.

20:07.407 --> 20:10.418
My husband nags me nonstop, you know.

20:10.418 --> 20:12.849
Then bring your husband next time.

20:12.849 --> 20:14.353
I'll make sure he has nothing to nag about...

20:14.353 --> 20:16.611
Please, that would be a disaster.

20:16.611 --> 20:18.577
Your phone keeps going off.

20:18.577 --> 20:20.830
Oh, sorry about that.

20:20.830 --> 20:22.901
Then I'm heading out.

20:22.901 --> 20:24.656
Ma'am.

20:24.656 --> 20:27.494
Ma'am.

20:32.945 --> 20:34.082
What are you doing?

20:34.082 --> 20:36.146
You must've thought about me at least once.

20:36.146 --> 20:37.363
Want to meet today?

20:37.363 --> 20:39.622
Wait...

20:39.622 --> 20:42.261
Did I get caught?

21:04.270 --> 21:06.487
I should've just told the truth.

21:06.487 --> 21:09.959
At least I wouldn't look this bad.

21:09.959 --> 21:11.950
I'm busy today.

21:11.950 --> 21:14.116
What happened that day was a mistake.

21:14.116 --> 21:16.501
Please don't be upset.

21:16.501 --> 21:19.554
[Send money via SoonmuPay]

21:20.418 --> 21:21.842
[To HeungJeongMangJeong]

21:21.842 --> 21:25.782
[To HeungJeongMangJeong]
15,000 won...

21:25.782 --> 21:28.955
Is that too much?

21:28.955 --> 21:30.512
Then...

21:30.512 --> 21:31.872
10,000 won.

21:31.872 --> 21:33.290
[Enter your SoonmuPay password]

21:33.290 --> 21:35.808
[10,000 won sent to HeungJeongMangJeong]
Could you check this machine?

21:35.808 --> 21:37.852
Sure.

21:39.135 --> 21:41.468
[10,000 won sent]
What?

21:42.702 --> 21:45.775
Is this punk seriously sending me money?

21:45.775 --> 21:48.219
What the...

21:48.219 --> 21:50.409
Does he have mayonnaise in his head
instead of a brain?

21:50.409 --> 21:52.672
You jerk!

21:52.672 --> 21:55.218
I got you now!

22:21.902 --> 22:23.845
Hello, this is Deukgeun Deukgeun Gym.

22:23.845 --> 22:27.571
Hello? Is this Mr. Lim Seung Jun?

22:29.197 --> 22:30.754
Yes, that's right.

22:30.754 --> 22:31.800
Who is this?

22:31.800 --> 22:33.614
This is the Soonmu Market operations team.

22:33.614 --> 22:35.384
You recently sold some comic books, correct?

22:35.384 --> 22:37.992
The buyer has filed a report.

22:37.992 --> 22:40.149
For inappropriate conduct
and fraud in a direct transaction.

22:40.149 --> 22:41.365
Do you admit to this?

22:41.365 --> 22:42.421
What?

22:42.421 --> 22:44.868
[Did you just send money?]
[Are you completely nuts?]

22:44.868 --> 22:48.641
[You think I'm a joke?]
[Why aren't you answering?]

22:50.864 --> 22:54.063
[Want me to break your neck?]
What is this supposed to be?

22:56.433 --> 22:57.824
- Ui Yeong.
- Yeah?

22:59.459 --> 23:02.916
Here's the tasting list and the recipes
for the whiskey pop-up.

23:02.916 --> 23:04.243
Okay.

23:04.243 --> 23:06.626
Oh, Sae Byeok.
Did you find the bartender for the event?

23:06.626 --> 23:08.016
Yes, I booked one.

23:08.016 --> 23:10.084
I'll send the profile by email.

23:10.084 --> 23:12.877
- Great.
- Alright.

23:14.290 --> 23:15.540
Dear HeungJeongMangJeong,

23:15.540 --> 23:18.347
I truly didn't mean to upset you.

23:18.347 --> 23:21.077
I'd like to apologize. Could we meet today?

23:21.077 --> 23:22.227
Oh, yeah?

23:22.227 --> 23:24.494
So you want to throw down the gauntlet?

23:24.494 --> 23:26.684
- That Soonmu Market?
- Yeah.

23:26.684 --> 23:30.534
Turns out it's not even recyclable.
Total trash!

23:30.534 --> 23:33.245
- The comic books?
- No. The seller.

23:33.245 --> 23:36.417
Looks like he skipped sex ed,
ethics class, and basic language lessons.

23:36.417 --> 23:39.723
I'm going to educate him today.

23:40.622 --> 23:42.016
[Song Tae Seop]

23:46.478 --> 23:49.325
Hello.

23:49.325 --> 23:51.618
Right now?

23:51.618 --> 23:55.165
You're coming to the office?

24:03.376 --> 24:06.616
Is this the only cafe around here?

24:07.962 --> 24:09.501
Your drinks are ready.

24:09.501 --> 24:11.432
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

24:11.432 --> 24:13.788
Thank you.

24:13.788 --> 24:15.885
Hey, do you have a girlfriend?

24:15.885 --> 24:18.191
- That's a secret.
- Come on, tell us.

24:18.191 --> 24:20.710
- She's the one who brought us all here today.
- Right.

24:20.710 --> 24:22.956
Come back three more times and I'll tell you.

24:22.956 --> 24:24.177
- Please.
- We have to come...

24:24.177 --> 24:26.323
Welcome...

24:27.594 --> 24:29.332
You're here... again?

24:29.332 --> 24:30.654
Yeah.

24:30.654 --> 24:33.671
Do the staff here pick and choose
which customers to welcome?

24:33.671 --> 24:36.176
Well, the staff are human too.

24:36.176 --> 24:38.081
Some customers are less welcome than others.

24:38.081 --> 24:39.928
Yeah?

24:39.928 --> 24:44.234
Four iced Americanos. To go.

24:46.348 --> 24:49.082
About last time, I ended up lying to you.

24:49.082 --> 24:52.392
You know I'm not her cousin, right?

24:52.392 --> 24:55.885
Yeah, it doesn't matter.

24:57.815 --> 24:59.226
Get the chocolate one.

24:59.226 --> 25:00.772
Ui Yeong loves chocolate.

25:00.772 --> 25:03.697
Then I'll take the carrot cake

25:03.697 --> 25:07.005
next to the chocolate one.

25:07.005 --> 25:09.149
There are a lot of people at her office.

25:09.149 --> 25:12.325
The chocolate one's on me.

25:12.325 --> 25:15.656
The cake's just for the two of us.

25:15.656 --> 25:18.549
Thanks for the freebie.

25:39.022 --> 25:40.479
Excuse me.

25:40.479 --> 25:43.273
- Oh, Mr. Song.
- Hello.

25:43.273 --> 25:45.537
You even brought cake.

25:45.537 --> 25:48.590
- Oh, thank you.
- Thanks.

25:50.032 --> 25:52.057
Shall we head upstairs?

25:52.057 --> 25:53.950
Okay.

25:53.950 --> 25:55.799
- I'll be back.
- Yeah.

25:55.799 --> 25:58.325
See you later.

26:39.437 --> 26:42.191
Is something wrong?

26:42.191 --> 26:44.671
There's something I'm stuck on.

26:44.671 --> 26:47.748
I thought talking it through with you
might help me sort it out.

26:47.748 --> 26:50.461
Okay, what is it?

26:52.048 --> 26:54.372
There's not much space we can really use here.

26:54.372 --> 26:56.645
Yeah. We've tried a few designs,

26:56.645 --> 26:59.865
but none of them really fit the room.

26:59.865 --> 27:01.649
What could we do...

27:01.649 --> 27:05.225
Let me run a little simulation.

27:06.602 --> 27:09.854
First I check in, come into the room,

27:09.854 --> 27:11.791
look around,

27:11.791 --> 27:13.458
and take photos.

27:13.458 --> 27:14.962
Maybe a selfie too.

27:14.962 --> 27:16.805
And then...

27:16.805 --> 27:18.927
I immediately

27:18.927 --> 27:21.878
- lie down.
- Oh.

27:21.878 --> 27:26.976
I roll around, lie this way, and that way.

27:26.976 --> 27:28.576
Basically I become one with the bed.

27:28.576 --> 27:30.982
- Maybe watch some TV.
- I see.

27:30.982 --> 27:32.367
So you're that type.

27:32.367 --> 27:35.558
And the only time I finally get up

27:35.558 --> 27:38.158
is when I'm hungry.

27:39.925 --> 27:41.142
Mr. Tae Seop,

27:41.142 --> 27:42.896
what if we did something on the bed?

27:42.896 --> 27:44.400
- On the bed?
- Yeah.

27:44.400 --> 27:45.710
Like those trays.

27:45.710 --> 27:48.600
People use them while sitting in bed.

27:55.923 --> 27:58.610
- A soban.
- A soban?

27:58.610 --> 28:01.001
When I was little,
I'd set one up on the bedding.

28:01.001 --> 28:04.074
I'd eat there or draw on it.

28:05.409 --> 28:07.192
That actually sounds nice.

28:07.192 --> 28:09.000
It wouldn't take up much space,

28:09.000 --> 28:10.725
and surprisingly,
it might go well with whiskey.

28:10.725 --> 28:12.559
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

28:12.559 --> 28:13.696
Then,

28:13.696 --> 28:16.749
the bedding should probably be a darker color.

28:16.749 --> 28:19.928
So spills won't stand out.

28:22.041 --> 28:23.985
Let's go with the soban as the main item

28:23.985 --> 28:25.583
and design around it.

28:25.583 --> 28:26.610
High five?

28:26.610 --> 28:29.276
- Yeah!
- Oh...

28:47.849 --> 28:50.441
Ms. Ui Yeong?

28:53.193 --> 28:55.666
She's not here?

28:56.499 --> 28:58.470
She said she was looking around the rooms.

28:58.470 --> 29:00.843
Where did she go?

29:01.438 --> 29:04.272
Ms. Ui Yeong.

29:05.386 --> 29:08.125
Did she go to another room?

29:33.356 --> 29:35.791
It's almost time for you
to get off work, right?

29:35.791 --> 29:36.881
Yes.

29:36.881 --> 29:39.567
I'll give you a ride home.

29:49.831 --> 29:50.867
[Seasons of Us]

29:50.867 --> 29:52.857
Looks like
"Seasons of Us" is being re-released.

29:52.857 --> 29:54.545
"Seasons of Us?"

29:54.545 --> 29:56.871
Is it good?

29:56.871 --> 29:58.015
You haven't seen it?

29:58.015 --> 30:00.148
That movie hit ten million viewers.

30:00.148 --> 30:03.214
I like that actress,
so I've seen it three times.

30:03.214 --> 30:04.938
Oh, really?

30:04.938 --> 30:06.675
Then I should definitely watch it.

30:06.675 --> 30:08.301
- Mr. Tae Seop.
- Yeah?

30:08.301 --> 30:10.285
We came up with the idea today,

30:10.285 --> 30:12.409
and once the pop-up installation is done,

30:12.409 --> 30:15.157
the important part is basically over, right?

30:15.157 --> 30:16.568
Yeah, pretty much.

30:16.568 --> 30:19.258
Then after we finish work that day,

30:19.258 --> 30:22.078
want to go see the late-night showing?

30:22.078 --> 30:24.176
That movie is really good.

30:24.176 --> 30:27.788
It'd be a shame to miss it.

30:27.788 --> 30:29.072
Sounds good.

30:29.072 --> 30:30.959
Let's grab something good to eat too.

30:30.959 --> 30:32.229
What do you like?

30:32.229 --> 30:33.754
Me?

30:33.754 --> 30:37.154
I'm not picky at all.
I eat pretty much anything.

30:38.281 --> 30:40.595
I can't wait.

30:49.644 --> 30:52.147
Did you just get off work?

30:52.147 --> 30:54.532
- Must've been a long day.
- Enough.

30:54.532 --> 30:56.796
This is your last chance.
Choose your words carefully.

30:56.796 --> 30:59.773
I'm really sorry for
not understanding how you felt.

30:59.773 --> 31:03.266
I'm not very experienced
with this kind of thing.

31:07.167 --> 31:09.353
Will this work?

31:16.203 --> 31:19.080
This punk...

31:19.080 --> 31:24.212
Didn't I say this was your last chance?

31:24.212 --> 31:26.150
Didn't I say this was

31:26.150 --> 31:27.756
- your last chance?
- Hey, calm down.

31:27.756 --> 31:29.530
- Let's talk this out.
- Are you an idiot?

31:29.530 --> 31:31.635
It's not even that expensive!

31:31.635 --> 31:33.593
What?

31:33.593 --> 31:38.340
Who do you think you are,
deciding what's expensive or not for me?

31:41.849 --> 31:43.507
Wait a second.

31:43.507 --> 31:46.413
When did I put a price on anything?

31:49.788 --> 31:53.815
I never imagined that was the price of...

31:53.815 --> 31:55.905
a ripped comic book.

31:55.905 --> 31:59.031
What kind of person do you think I am?

32:01.351 --> 32:04.691
I'm a trainer. I don't eat fried food.

32:04.691 --> 32:06.261
I worked hard for this body.

32:06.261 --> 32:08.695
Yeah, you should protect those nice muscles.

32:08.695 --> 32:10.673
I'm Jung Hyun Min, thirty years old.

32:10.673 --> 32:11.912
I work at a company.

32:11.912 --> 32:13.662
But I've been wondering...

32:13.662 --> 32:16.498
Why did you clean my place
before you left that day?

32:26.632 --> 32:28.263
Well...

32:28.263 --> 32:31.476
If only the books were put away,
that'd look suspicious.

32:57.064 --> 32:58.381
I mean...

32:58.381 --> 33:00.935
if I'd just taken the comics and left,
that would've looked weird.

33:00.935 --> 33:04.215
So I just cleaned up while I was at it.

33:21.573 --> 33:23.431
So you can eat this, right?

33:23.431 --> 33:28.204
I'm pretty good at peeling things, by the way.

33:49.880 --> 33:51.058
By the way,

33:51.058 --> 33:54.800
once you sleep with someone,
do you lose interest in them?

33:57.198 --> 33:59.222
No, not at all.

33:59.222 --> 34:01.035
Lower your voice.

34:01.035 --> 34:02.932
Oh, thank goodness.

34:02.932 --> 34:05.556
Because I really like you.

34:05.556 --> 34:08.016
What do you think of me?

34:08.016 --> 34:10.506
In this situation, you're really asking that?

34:10.506 --> 34:12.730
Yeah, the misunderstanding's cleared up.

34:12.730 --> 34:14.407
Your bruise will heal soon.

34:14.407 --> 34:17.037
We can even eat this whole chicken
without fighting.

34:17.037 --> 34:20.410
Everything feels pretty great right now.

34:20.410 --> 34:23.690
So... why don't we get to know each other?

34:45.125 --> 34:46.262
Mr. Tae Seop,

34:46.262 --> 34:49.768
you're coming
for the pop-up installation today, right?

34:52.180 --> 34:55.140
Yes, see you soon.

34:55.890 --> 34:57.207
Hey, watch the back.

34:57.207 --> 34:59.200
Be careful.

34:59.200 --> 35:02.527
You're going to break everything.

35:03.617 --> 35:06.756
A white shirt on installation day?

35:06.756 --> 35:08.788
- Oh, good timing.
- What?

35:08.788 --> 35:11.574
You know that professor in Hannam-dong
who bought the desk from us?

35:11.574 --> 35:14.753
He called asking if we could move the meeting
to tonight.

35:14.753 --> 35:16.464
But I have to take Sua to the hospital,

35:16.464 --> 35:18.053
- so can you handle it?
- What?

35:18.053 --> 35:19.734
I can't, I have to go to the hotel.

35:19.734 --> 35:21.448
He's a regular. Let's do him a favor.

35:21.448 --> 35:23.158
He says it's because of
his kid's academy schedule.

35:23.158 --> 35:26.079
You can head over after the meeting.

35:27.199 --> 35:29.787
Then tell him to come as early as possible.

35:29.787 --> 35:31.873
Jin Su!

35:33.001 --> 35:34.058
Yes?

35:34.058 --> 35:36.185
I'll head over after the meeting,
so let them know,

35:36.185 --> 35:37.902
and send me some photos
during the installation.

35:37.902 --> 35:39.035
- Oh, photos?
- Yeah.

35:39.035 --> 35:40.955
Got it.

35:42.241 --> 35:44.865
That intern reminds me of Senior Ui Yeong.

35:44.865 --> 35:46.455
Acts all innocent, but she's sly.

35:46.455 --> 35:51.006
Looks kind,
but she's actually hard to deal with.

35:51.006 --> 35:53.363
You've changed your salary, your car,

35:53.363 --> 35:55.533
even your taste in liquor.

35:55.533 --> 35:58.183
So why is your taste in women still the same?

35:58.183 --> 36:00.403
Yeah?

36:00.403 --> 36:03.433
Stop chasing a lost cause.

36:03.433 --> 36:05.330
There are plenty of girls
who'd say yes if I introduced you.

36:05.330 --> 36:08.349
You really have no plans
to go back to the firm?

36:20.783 --> 36:21.813
Okay.

36:21.813 --> 36:25.342
Alright, let's go. One, two, three.

36:31.157 --> 36:32.787
- Hello.
- Oh, hi.

36:32.787 --> 36:34.601
Is the CEO not coming?

36:34.601 --> 36:37.052
He couldn't make it
because of a client meeting.

36:37.052 --> 36:38.753
Didn't he let you know?

36:38.753 --> 36:41.569
I didn't...

36:41.569 --> 36:42.611
get a message.

36:42.611 --> 36:45.444
He must've forgotten. It happens a lot.

36:45.444 --> 36:47.497
I see.

36:49.444 --> 36:51.921
Excuse me,
which floor should we take all this to?

36:51.921 --> 36:53.921
Please move everything to the L floor.

36:53.921 --> 36:56.247
This way, please.

36:59.820 --> 37:02.165
Watch your step.

37:02.165 --> 37:04.173
Take it slow.

37:06.263 --> 37:08.709
Over there? Okay.

37:12.726 --> 37:15.079
You didn't have to move all of it.

37:15.079 --> 37:17.507
I think I grabbed too much.

37:17.507 --> 37:19.078
- Let me hold that for you.
- Thank you.

37:19.078 --> 37:20.917
This is pretty heavy.

37:20.917 --> 37:22.615
Yeah.

37:22.615 --> 37:24.695
This way.

37:24.695 --> 37:28.108
She sure has no problem
accepting help from others.

37:28.108 --> 37:29.892
See you tomorrow at six.

37:29.892 --> 37:31.765
Okay.

37:34.344 --> 37:36.735
- Welcome.
- Hello.

37:36.735 --> 37:39.509
- Are you ready to order?
- Yeah.

37:39.509 --> 37:42.652
Ten hot Americanos,

37:42.652 --> 37:44.962
ten iced ones,

37:44.962 --> 37:48.615
and this hot chocolate here.

37:48.615 --> 37:50.629
And I'll take all of these.

37:50.629 --> 37:51.986
All of them?

37:51.986 --> 37:53.112
Yes.

37:53.112 --> 37:55.332
Ji Su...

38:02.864 --> 38:06.204
- Come again.
- Thanks.

38:10.691 --> 38:12.365
Excuse me.

38:12.365 --> 38:13.934
Is the place you're going nearby?

38:13.934 --> 38:15.607
Well...

38:15.607 --> 38:16.810
The Hills Hotel.

38:16.810 --> 38:19.409
Someone I like is working late there.

38:20.380 --> 38:22.607
A hotel?

38:33.721 --> 38:35.592
Here, just leave it here.

38:35.592 --> 38:38.034
- Oh, okay.
- Yeah.

38:38.034 --> 38:40.255
Alright then.

38:40.255 --> 38:42.727
- Thanks.
- Yeah.

38:46.632 --> 38:48.329
What are you doing here?

38:48.329 --> 38:49.694
Delivery.

38:49.694 --> 38:50.974
You deliver now?

38:50.974 --> 38:52.716
Just today.

38:52.716 --> 38:53.966
- Working late?
- Yeah...

38:53.966 --> 38:55.309
I've got that event I told you about.

38:55.309 --> 38:58.124
Everyone, help yourselves to some coffee.

38:58.124 --> 39:00.068
- Kang Do Hyun?
- Have some coffee.

39:00.068 --> 39:02.584
Sae Byeok! Over here.

39:02.584 --> 39:04.381
Attorney Kang,

39:04.381 --> 39:06.727
what are you doing here?

39:06.727 --> 39:08.025
Well...

39:08.025 --> 39:10.985
It looked like you were working late,
so I brought some coffee.

39:10.985 --> 39:13.629
Since it's late, I got you hot chocolate.

39:13.629 --> 39:15.753
Hold on, I'll find it.

39:15.753 --> 39:18.290
- Just a moment.
- I'm really fine.

39:18.290 --> 39:22.129
Why didn't he mark this?

39:23.690 --> 39:26.771
Hey, Attorney Kang.

39:26.771 --> 39:29.340
Did I ever ask for this?

39:29.340 --> 39:30.965
No, right?

39:30.965 --> 39:33.231
Hold on a second.

39:35.379 --> 39:37.205
Kang Do Hyun,

39:37.205 --> 39:38.322
you can talk tomorrow.

39:38.322 --> 39:40.375
There are people from other companies here.

39:40.375 --> 39:43.593
Come on, it's just coffee.
What's wrong with buying coffee?

39:43.593 --> 39:46.916
If the person receiving it feels uncomfortable,

39:46.916 --> 39:48.660
you should think about that too.

39:48.660 --> 39:51.050
You're partly responsible
for this situation too.

39:51.050 --> 39:52.105
What?

39:52.105 --> 39:54.890
You don't even feel sorry toward me?

39:54.890 --> 39:57.137
For what?

39:57.137 --> 39:58.624
You know...

39:58.624 --> 40:01.267
Ui Yeong, because of you,

40:01.267 --> 40:05.070
Sae Byeok feels uncomfortable around me.

40:05.070 --> 40:07.136
Why...

40:08.163 --> 40:12.651
Why are you acting like you like me now?

40:12.651 --> 40:14.991
Just to get in the way of my love...

40:14.991 --> 40:17.237
What?

40:17.237 --> 40:19.570
Well...

40:25.688 --> 40:27.935
I'm leaving.

40:27.935 --> 40:31.608
I'll take all of this with me.

40:32.795 --> 40:35.335
Oh, be careful!

40:37.082 --> 40:39.355
Oh my!

40:40.642 --> 40:42.748
Hey, are you okay?

40:42.748 --> 40:45.522
- It's hot...
- Let's go to the hospital.

40:48.372 --> 40:50.364
Get something to wipe this up!

40:50.364 --> 40:52.644
Oh gosh...

40:54.658 --> 40:57.259
Attorney Kang,

40:57.259 --> 41:00.890
I think you're seriously mistaken
about something.

41:00.890 --> 41:02.761
It's not because of her.

41:02.761 --> 41:05.057
It's just that... people like you,

41:05.057 --> 41:08.655
who make such a big deal out of
their own feelings,

41:08.655 --> 41:13.225
make me uncomfortable.

41:13.225 --> 41:14.796
Yeah...

41:14.796 --> 41:15.980
I actually hate that.

41:15.980 --> 41:17.864
Not as a friend, not as a coworker.

41:17.864 --> 41:21.057
So please...

41:21.057 --> 41:23.897
don't like me.

41:29.422 --> 41:32.488
Hey, get this one first.

41:39.698 --> 41:41.412
Hey, Jin Su.

41:41.412 --> 41:43.896
- Call the boss.
- Yeah, okay.

41:43.896 --> 41:47.327
[Under Construction]

41:51.671 --> 41:55.427
Sorry, I'm a bit late. Something came up,
so I'm heading out now.

41:59.721 --> 42:02.374
[Jin Su]
[Sir, we've got a problem.]

42:07.500 --> 42:09.524
Sir, we've got a problem.

42:09.524 --> 42:12.467
You should come take a look.

42:12.467 --> 42:14.733
Why is this...

42:17.114 --> 42:19.138
Fortunately, it's nothing serious.

42:19.138 --> 42:21.980
Thank you.

42:26.173 --> 42:28.973
- Here's your receipt.
- Thank you.

42:43.636 --> 42:47.043
You should've been careful
with even a single drop.

42:47.043 --> 42:49.274
I'm sorry. It was my mistake.

42:49.274 --> 42:52.298
Everyone else worked hard the whole time.

42:52.298 --> 42:54.135
No, it wasn't your fault.

42:54.135 --> 42:57.111
Something unexpected happened.

42:57.111 --> 42:59.560
Let's finish it again with a darker oil.

42:59.560 --> 43:00.777
All of the furniture?

43:00.777 --> 43:02.350
If we want the colors to match, we have to.

43:02.350 --> 43:04.075
Let's hurry and finish today.

43:04.075 --> 43:05.990
Yes.

43:34.598 --> 43:38.277
You have to spread it like this.

43:38.277 --> 43:41.058
[Emergency Medical Center]

43:41.058 --> 43:42.560
Well...

43:42.560 --> 43:45.397
I think I should head back to the hotel.

43:45.397 --> 43:48.236
You're going back to the hotel
in that condition?

43:48.236 --> 43:51.101
I rushed out, so I think I dropped my phone.

43:51.101 --> 43:53.405
And they must be in chaos
trying to fix the furniture.

43:53.405 --> 43:56.167
I should go check.

44:00.101 --> 44:02.552
Call them first.

44:02.552 --> 44:04.674
Okay.

44:11.554 --> 44:14.334
Where should I move this?

44:15.688 --> 44:19.426
CEO Song came and is helping fix things.

44:19.426 --> 44:21.167
Oh, he's there?

44:21.167 --> 44:22.987
We're almost done anyway,

44:22.987 --> 44:25.263
just get some rest at home.

44:25.263 --> 44:26.440
You were hurt, right?

44:26.440 --> 44:28.233
I'm really sorry.

44:28.233 --> 44:31.610
Hey, why are you apologizing?

44:31.610 --> 44:34.087
Alright then. I'll head home today.

44:34.087 --> 44:36.384
- See you tomorrow.
- Yeah, see you tomorrow.

44:36.384 --> 44:38.586
Okay.

44:40.559 --> 44:42.892
Let's just go home.

44:42.892 --> 44:46.350
Before we go, let's stop by one place.

44:46.350 --> 44:49.454
Oh, I meant to ask earlier
but things were hectic.

44:49.454 --> 44:51.071
Why are there two helmets?

44:51.071 --> 44:52.418
One for me, one for you.

44:52.418 --> 44:55.791
You said you wanted to try riding a motorcycle.

45:11.538 --> 45:13.261
This feels so good.

45:13.261 --> 45:14.548
What?

45:14.548 --> 45:17.348
I said it feels great!

45:18.295 --> 45:21.668
It feels like a huge weight
just lifted off my chest.

45:31.682 --> 45:34.012
When Ms. Ui Yeong stepped in to stop him,

45:34.012 --> 45:36.403
that guy started complaining
right in front of everyone.

45:36.403 --> 45:38.480
Saying things would've been fine
if she wasn't there.

45:38.480 --> 45:40.875
What else could that mean?

45:40.875 --> 45:42.619
A love triangle.

45:42.619 --> 45:44.318
That can't be.

45:44.318 --> 45:45.363
Come on.

45:45.363 --> 45:47.535
Attorney Kang likes Ms. Sae Byeok.

45:47.535 --> 45:48.783
If Ms. Ui Yeong's getting in the way,

45:48.783 --> 45:51.299
then either they're dating
or at least something's going on.

45:51.299 --> 45:53.771
You've never even dated. What would you know?

45:53.771 --> 45:56.799
Even so, they don't match.

45:56.799 --> 45:58.244
Look.

45:58.244 --> 46:01.044
That's the lawyer from earlier.

46:16.432 --> 46:18.915
Mr. Song Tae Seop?

46:18.915 --> 46:20.920
Attorney Kang,

46:20.920 --> 46:24.066
can we talk for a moment?

46:25.688 --> 46:28.188
About what?

46:29.329 --> 46:32.393
If this is about the furniture,
I had unavoidable circumstances...

46:32.393 --> 46:35.186
That made me angry too, but we're handling it.

46:35.186 --> 46:37.890
If it comes down to it,
I could hold you liable for breach of contract.

46:37.890 --> 46:40.594
The responsible party is obvious.

46:40.594 --> 46:44.670
You wrote the contract yourself,
so you know what it says.

46:44.670 --> 46:46.694
Are you threatening me right now?

46:46.694 --> 46:49.353
Threats fall under Article 283
of the criminal code...

46:49.353 --> 46:50.783
I'm not sure

46:50.783 --> 46:53.363
if this counts as a threat,

46:53.363 --> 46:56.263
but I like Ms. Ui Yeong.

46:56.263 --> 46:59.114
- What did you say?
- She's important to me.

46:59.114 --> 47:01.914
So be careful from now on.

47:03.606 --> 47:04.732
So...

47:04.732 --> 47:05.885
this is all because of her?

47:05.885 --> 47:08.628
Your words, your actions, even your thoughts.

47:08.628 --> 47:11.428
Watch them.

47:32.788 --> 47:36.054
[Sorry, I'm a bit late. Something came up...]

47:49.903 --> 47:52.430
[Song Tae Seop]

47:57.574 --> 48:00.374
[Song Tae Seop]
[Ms. Ui Yeong]

48:13.672 --> 48:15.842
What is this?

48:15.842 --> 48:18.062
Isn't this just instant ramen?

48:18.062 --> 48:19.639
Why is it so good?

48:19.639 --> 48:21.799
Because the setting isn't ordinary.

48:21.799 --> 48:25.452
It feels like it's soothing your soul, right?

48:33.850 --> 48:36.256
I'm full.

48:36.990 --> 48:41.816
By the way, did you like that lawyer too?

48:41.816 --> 48:43.080
Do you fall for guys that fast?

48:43.080 --> 48:44.794
Hey, no.

48:44.794 --> 48:46.544
That guy was just...

48:46.544 --> 48:48.004
a passing thing.

48:48.004 --> 48:50.824
Your taste in men is really...

48:50.824 --> 48:53.409
And don't trust that guy you kissed too much.

48:53.409 --> 48:56.988
All this chaos today
and he didn't even show up.

48:56.988 --> 49:00.341
He's the boss. He must be busy.

49:00.341 --> 49:02.718
But you must be tired too.

49:02.718 --> 49:04.742
You said you worked today, right?

49:04.742 --> 49:06.932
Is the cafe job hard?

49:06.932 --> 49:11.148
If you did more movies or dramas,
you'd probably make better money.

49:11.148 --> 49:13.812
I don't act to make money.

49:13.812 --> 49:15.092
I just do it because I like it.

49:15.092 --> 49:18.429
Still, if you love acting,
why not make money from it too?

49:18.429 --> 49:20.396
And it wouldn't hurt to become famous.

49:20.396 --> 49:21.854
There'd be a price for that.

49:21.854 --> 49:25.714
Like giving up moments like this.

49:26.749 --> 49:28.701
To me, this view is

49:28.701 --> 49:31.576
more comforting

49:32.182 --> 49:35.082
than money or fame.

49:44.664 --> 49:46.367
Thank you.

49:46.367 --> 49:48.151
- Have this.
- Thanks.

49:48.151 --> 49:49.857
You worked hard today, staying this late.

49:49.857 --> 49:51.160
No, not at all.

49:51.160 --> 49:54.625
Thank you so much for helping us.

49:56.011 --> 49:59.725
Did you want to say something?

49:59.725 --> 50:00.822
Nothing.

50:00.822 --> 50:04.028
Your arms and shoulders might feel sore,
so put on a patch before bed.

50:04.028 --> 50:06.178
Okay. Thank you for today.

50:06.178 --> 50:08.718
- You too.
- Yeah.

50:45.204 --> 50:46.961
They say sadness dissolves in water.

50:46.961 --> 50:48.608
Does anger evaporate?

50:48.608 --> 50:50.330
The wind just blew it all away.

50:50.330 --> 50:52.171
Let me know if you want to go for another ride.

50:52.171 --> 50:55.045
And at night, I make drinks at the cafe too.

50:55.045 --> 50:57.742
Come by sometime. I'll take good care of you.

50:57.742 --> 51:00.668
Here, my number.

51:16.298 --> 51:18.648
Mr. Tae Seop? What are you doing here?

51:18.648 --> 51:20.855
You left your phone.

51:20.855 --> 51:23.276
Oh, I thought
I'd have to come back for it tomorrow.

51:23.276 --> 51:24.313
Thank you.

51:24.313 --> 51:28.858
Can we talk for a moment? It won't take long.

51:28.858 --> 51:31.009
I'll talk to him for a bit.

51:31.009 --> 51:32.116
You go ahead.

51:32.116 --> 51:35.055
- Thanks for today.
- Alright.

51:37.705 --> 51:39.422
What happened to your arm?

51:39.422 --> 51:41.679
Did you go to the hospital?

51:41.679 --> 51:43.603
I got burned by some coffee,

51:43.603 --> 51:46.226
but they said it's nothing serious.

51:46.226 --> 51:50.363
I heard from Sae Byeok
that you handled things at the site.

51:50.363 --> 51:51.573
Thank you.

51:51.573 --> 51:53.237
If I'd gotten there a little sooner,

51:53.237 --> 51:55.618
it probably wouldn't have gotten this bad.

51:55.618 --> 51:59.117
You had something to deal with, that's all.

52:00.095 --> 52:02.589
But honestly...

52:02.589 --> 52:06.922
I did wait for you.

52:07.648 --> 52:09.186
I'm sorry.

52:09.186 --> 52:11.837
From now on, I won't be late

52:11.837 --> 52:14.845
or keep you waiting.

52:17.402 --> 52:21.379
Do you have any photos from the site?

52:21.379 --> 52:24.626
- Want to see?
- Yes.

52:24.626 --> 52:26.232
Here.

52:27.979 --> 52:30.623
It's even better than I imagined.

52:30.623 --> 52:32.836
Not bad, right?

52:41.797 --> 52:43.755
I got home safely.

52:43.755 --> 52:46.555
Get some good rest tonight.

52:54.650 --> 52:55.740
- Hyun Min,
- Yes?

52:55.740 --> 52:58.844
- everything's ready, right?
- I think we're all set.

52:58.844 --> 53:00.136
- Ms. Ui Yeong.
- Yes?

53:00.136 --> 53:02.854
The bartender we booked just called.

53:02.854 --> 53:04.771
He can't make it.
Someone in his family is sick.

53:04.771 --> 53:06.947
- What?
- On the day of the event?

53:06.947 --> 53:08.085
Yes.

53:08.085 --> 53:10.469
But we really need a bartender.

53:10.469 --> 53:13.046
What do we do?

53:13.046 --> 53:15.972
Guys, give me a second.

53:16.571 --> 53:20.587
The props you made fit our hotel perfectly.

53:20.587 --> 53:25.080
I especially love this octagonal soban.

53:25.080 --> 53:26.964
I heard the soban and bedding idea

53:26.964 --> 53:29.850
was something you and Ms. Ui Yeong
came up with together.

53:29.850 --> 53:32.500
You two have great chemistry.

53:32.500 --> 53:34.207
Thank you.

53:34.207 --> 53:35.604
And the guest rooms

53:35.604 --> 53:39.797
will first be used as a trial
by brand representatives and VIP guests.

53:39.797 --> 53:43.581
After that, we'll reorganize them
and open them to regular guests.

53:43.581 --> 53:46.645
Orders placed through the pop-up
will be collected

53:46.645 --> 53:48.311
and passed along through Ms. Ui Yeong.

53:48.311 --> 53:52.125
- Thank you. We appreciate it.
- Thank you.

53:52.125 --> 53:53.988
And this is...

53:53.988 --> 53:57.243
a small gift for the staff who worked so hard.

53:57.243 --> 53:59.068
- Oh.
- Wow.

53:59.068 --> 54:01.595
- The team is going to love this.
- Right.

54:01.595 --> 54:03.313
You can use this room.

54:03.313 --> 54:05.283
We'll call you when the pop-up opens.

54:05.283 --> 54:07.048
- Please get some rest first.
- Okay.

54:07.048 --> 54:09.927
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

54:17.479 --> 54:20.190
We were in a hurry,
so I just had him wear one of our uniforms.

54:20.190 --> 54:22.520
Yeah, it couldn't be helped.

54:22.520 --> 54:25.126
We did our best.

54:28.248 --> 54:30.601
How do I look?

54:30.601 --> 54:33.674
- Is it too short?
- Wow.

54:53.626 --> 54:57.011
The bartender experience booth
is very popular right now.

54:57.011 --> 54:58.831
It's great.

54:59.455 --> 55:02.408
If you purchase any two items...

55:15.566 --> 55:18.366
Here you go.

55:31.252 --> 55:33.198
Hey.

55:35.520 --> 55:37.065
My wrist is about to fall off.

55:37.065 --> 55:39.291
I said I'd make you a drink,

55:39.291 --> 55:41.948
not serve all these people.

55:41.948 --> 55:43.352
I'll make it up to you.

55:43.352 --> 55:44.552
But seriously,

55:44.552 --> 55:47.163
did this place really get designed
by that guy, Song Tae Seop?

55:47.163 --> 55:49.803
Yeah. Isn't it amazing?

55:50.942 --> 55:52.884
Oh, Mr. Tae Seop!

55:52.884 --> 55:55.272
Ms. Ui Yeong.

55:55.993 --> 55:57.243
Can I get you something?

55:57.243 --> 55:58.781
No, I'm good.

55:58.781 --> 56:01.561
- Did you look around?
- Yes, it's incredible.

56:01.561 --> 56:04.911
And it seems like
the brand representatives are really pleased.

56:04.911 --> 56:06.628
That's a relief.

56:06.628 --> 56:08.068
If you have a moment...

56:08.068 --> 56:09.132
Sir,

56:09.132 --> 56:10.483
could you greet the guests over there too?

56:10.483 --> 56:11.825
Oh, yes.

56:11.825 --> 56:14.011
Just a second.

56:17.711 --> 56:20.189
Son Jeong A!

56:20.189 --> 56:21.987
What's with her?

56:21.987 --> 56:26.086
This brand has been the main sponsor
of the Geumsang Arts Awards for years.

56:26.086 --> 56:28.903
She's just beautiful.

56:28.903 --> 56:30.852
I'm a huge fan of hers.

56:30.852 --> 56:34.064
She doesn't even act anymore.

56:34.064 --> 56:37.384
She's just a celebrity now.

56:37.384 --> 56:41.044
Oh gosh, did you see that? She winked at me!

56:42.435 --> 56:45.682
You saw that, right? She winked at me.

57:18.727 --> 57:20.665
- There you are.
- Oh, hi.

57:20.665 --> 57:23.895
You looked pretty busy greeting everyone.

57:23.895 --> 57:25.045
Yeah...

57:25.045 --> 57:26.893
But things have settled down now.

57:26.893 --> 57:27.922
I know.

57:27.922 --> 57:31.341
Thanks to you,
everything seems to have gone well.

58:01.116 --> 58:02.800
Ms. Ui Yeong.

58:02.800 --> 58:03.846
Yes?

58:03.846 --> 58:05.870
About that thing
we didn't get to do last time...

58:05.870 --> 58:07.494
- Ms. Ui Yeong!
- Yes?

58:07.494 --> 58:10.538
Some people didn't seem to know
about the after-party tonight.

58:10.538 --> 58:12.288
You did send the notice, right?

58:12.288 --> 58:13.322
Oh, right.

58:13.322 --> 58:15.961
Geez...

58:15.961 --> 58:17.711
You're coming too, right?

58:17.711 --> 58:19.399
I actually don't drink...

58:19.399 --> 58:21.656
It's at the cafe right up front.

58:21.656 --> 58:25.374
You and your team are coming, right?

58:25.374 --> 58:28.825
Even if I don't drink,
I always make it to the after-party.

58:28.825 --> 58:31.215
That's when a project really feels finished.

58:31.215 --> 58:32.680
- You have to come.
- Of course.

58:32.680 --> 58:35.500
- See you later.
- Promise!

58:45.621 --> 58:46.853
You worked really hard.

58:46.853 --> 58:48.422
You too.

58:48.422 --> 58:50.085
- Hello.
- Hello.

58:50.085 --> 58:52.025
- Great work today.
- Thank you.

58:52.025 --> 58:54.003
- Oh, here they come.
- Hello.

58:54.003 --> 58:56.644
Great work today.

58:56.644 --> 58:59.114
Have a seat.

58:59.114 --> 59:01.845
You're everywhere I go.

59:01.845 --> 59:04.135
I'm exactly where I should be.

59:04.135 --> 59:07.045
Ever think you might be the one butting in?

59:07.045 --> 59:08.468
Jin Su, here.

59:08.468 --> 59:10.436
I love company dinners.

59:10.436 --> 59:12.340
Hey, switch seats with me.

59:12.340 --> 59:14.184
Mr. Song!

59:14.184 --> 59:15.565
Where are you going? Over here.

59:15.565 --> 59:17.642
- No, I...
- I saved you a seat.

59:17.642 --> 59:19.801
You should join us for a drink.

59:19.801 --> 59:21.961
Just have one here first,
and you can move seats later.

59:21.961 --> 59:25.231
Great work today, sir.

59:25.231 --> 59:27.582
Wait, where is Mr. Lee Eun Ho?

59:27.582 --> 59:29.959
He couldn't make it today.
Something came up with his child.

59:29.959 --> 59:31.220
Thank you.

59:31.220 --> 59:33.566
Thank you.

59:36.276 --> 59:38.287
- How about a drink, sir?
- I don't drink alcohol.

59:38.287 --> 59:40.591
Just hold the glass.

59:40.591 --> 59:41.962
♪ Your glass is filling up ♪

59:41.962 --> 59:44.819
- One second.
- Drink up.

59:44.819 --> 59:46.657
Mr. Ji Su, have a drink with us too.

59:46.657 --> 59:49.993
- Have a seat!
- Do you want another drink?

59:49.993 --> 59:51.669
Mrs. Na Ri, have a drink too.

59:51.669 --> 59:53.803
You have to drink on a day like this.

59:53.803 --> 59:55.983
And...

59:55.983 --> 59:59.576
- Let me pour you a drink.
- Thanks.

59:59.576 --> 01:00:02.020
- Great work today.
- Thank you.

01:00:02.020 --> 01:00:03.117
Alright,

01:00:03.117 --> 01:00:05.964
fill up your glasses.

01:00:05.964 --> 01:00:08.402
Let's meet again soon
on another project, in good health.

01:00:08.402 --> 01:00:10.540
- Cheers!
- Cheers.

01:00:10.540 --> 01:00:12.058
- Thank you.
- Thank you for your hard work.

01:00:12.058 --> 01:00:15.131
Thank you for your effort.

01:00:21.024 --> 01:00:24.470
This is so sweet.

01:00:24.470 --> 01:00:26.789
Let's start the Rabbit Game!

01:00:26.789 --> 01:00:28.961
- Umchi-chi, umchi-chi.
- Umchi-chi, umchi-chi.

01:00:28.961 --> 01:00:31.171
- Bunny, bunny.
- Carrot, carrot!

01:00:31.171 --> 01:00:33.871
Where is Attorney Kang?

01:00:33.871 --> 01:00:36.008
He probably won't come.

01:00:36.008 --> 01:00:38.708
How would you know that?

01:00:38.708 --> 01:00:41.028
Have a drink.

01:00:41.901 --> 01:00:43.778
Everyone except Yu Been, let's raise a glass.

01:00:43.778 --> 01:00:45.135
Sounds good.

01:00:45.135 --> 01:00:47.431
This is so fun.

01:00:50.278 --> 01:00:52.102
But Mr. Ji Su,

01:00:52.102 --> 01:00:54.160
what exactly do you do? Are you a bartender?

01:00:54.160 --> 01:00:56.798
Oh, his real job?

01:00:56.798 --> 01:00:58.348
He's an actor.

01:00:58.348 --> 01:00:59.979
Seriously?

01:00:59.979 --> 01:01:01.289
I do theater,

01:01:01.289 --> 01:01:03.313
and I've worked a lot of part time jobs,

01:01:03.313 --> 01:01:05.440
so I picked up things like this.

01:01:05.440 --> 01:01:08.380
I knew it. You've got a different aura.

01:01:08.380 --> 01:01:10.070
Do you have a fan club?

01:01:10.070 --> 01:01:13.830
If not, I'll start one today.
I'll be the president.

01:01:15.930 --> 01:01:17.658
Don't be the president. Be the audience.

01:01:17.658 --> 01:01:19.836
I'll invite all of you.

01:01:19.836 --> 01:01:22.762
- Come see my play.
- I love that!

01:01:23.822 --> 01:01:26.910
- Promise!
- Yeah!

01:01:30.815 --> 01:01:34.082
- You better keep that promise.
- Of course.

01:01:36.078 --> 01:01:39.585
Come on, let's drink!

01:01:39.585 --> 01:01:40.775
Come on.

01:01:40.775 --> 01:01:42.614
You too.

01:01:43.729 --> 01:01:46.729
Drink up!

01:01:46.729 --> 01:01:49.579
Oh, your place is that way...

01:01:49.579 --> 01:01:52.129
So you usually drive on Gangbyeonbuk-ro, huh?

01:01:52.129 --> 01:01:55.577
Gang... Gangbyeon...

01:01:55.577 --> 01:01:58.038
Where exactly is Gangbyeon?

01:02:14.460 --> 01:02:16.758
You usually get drunk after only two drinks.

01:02:16.758 --> 01:02:18.171
Sir...

01:02:18.171 --> 01:02:20.528
How many fingers do you see?

01:02:20.528 --> 01:02:25.154
Hey, when did your hand grow six fingers?

01:02:27.427 --> 01:02:29.908
Hold on.

01:02:29.908 --> 01:02:32.915
I'm going to get some air.

01:02:34.639 --> 01:02:37.099
Be careful.

01:02:38.985 --> 01:02:41.765
Excuse me for a second.

01:02:43.999 --> 01:02:46.119
Let me just...

01:02:54.722 --> 01:02:56.722
Mr. Tae Seop?

01:02:56.722 --> 01:02:58.672
Mr. Tae Seop.

01:02:58.672 --> 01:03:00.082
Hey.

01:03:00.082 --> 01:03:02.835
Are you okay?

01:03:04.350 --> 01:03:07.287
No, I'm not.

01:03:07.287 --> 01:03:09.454
My stomach...

01:03:09.454 --> 01:03:11.651
It feels like it's turning.

01:03:11.651 --> 01:03:12.841
Oh my...

01:03:12.841 --> 01:03:15.925
I'll run and get a hangover remedy.

01:03:15.925 --> 01:03:18.481
Just wait here a second, okay?

01:03:18.481 --> 01:03:21.626
No. Don't go.

01:03:21.626 --> 01:03:22.651
What?

01:03:22.651 --> 01:03:26.547
I mean... you're right here,

01:03:26.547 --> 01:03:28.118
but I can't hold on to you.

01:03:28.118 --> 01:03:31.278
So my stomach keeps turning.

01:03:42.503 --> 01:03:44.976
You can't go.

01:03:57.221 --> 01:04:00.814
So this is your cute drunk side.

01:04:07.521 --> 01:04:09.447
Mr. Tae Seop,

01:04:09.447 --> 01:04:11.870
I'm not going anywhere.

01:04:11.870 --> 01:04:13.155
So...

01:04:13.155 --> 01:04:16.861
you don't have to hold on that tight.

01:04:17.528 --> 01:04:19.234
Oh, okay.

01:04:19.234 --> 01:04:21.867
But Ms. Ui Yeong,

01:04:22.822 --> 01:04:27.562
do you still want to go on that date with me?

01:04:27.562 --> 01:04:31.018
Yes, I do.

01:04:31.018 --> 01:04:33.398
Then...

01:04:34.131 --> 01:04:36.844
do you want to go somewhere

01:04:36.844 --> 01:04:40.117
and have one more drink just the two of us?

01:04:40.117 --> 01:04:42.917
Right now?

01:04:46.949 --> 01:04:49.543
Okay.

01:04:49.543 --> 01:04:52.294
Then I'll quickly grab my bag and come back.

01:04:52.294 --> 01:04:55.814
Just wait here a second, okay?

01:04:57.425 --> 01:05:00.778
Don't go anywhere. Stay right here.

01:05:00.778 --> 01:05:03.499
I'll be right back.

01:05:27.214 --> 01:05:29.860
Mr. Tae Seop!

01:05:32.080 --> 01:05:34.631
Mr. Tae Seop, you can't fall asleep here.

01:05:34.631 --> 01:05:36.915
Wake up.

01:05:36.915 --> 01:05:40.548
It's dangerous to sleep here.

01:05:40.548 --> 01:05:44.901
We said we'd go for another round.

01:05:50.063 --> 01:05:52.736
What is this?

01:06:30.780 --> 01:06:33.527
Where am I?

01:06:33.527 --> 01:06:35.770
Hold on.

01:06:35.770 --> 01:06:39.879
What is this? Why is this black?

01:06:43.083 --> 01:06:44.827
What?

01:06:44.827 --> 01:06:46.378
Oh no...

01:06:46.378 --> 01:06:48.838
Did I sleep with him?

01:06:48.838 --> 01:06:51.658
Did I do it?

01:07:04.319 --> 01:07:06.974
What are you doing?

01:07:06.974 --> 01:07:10.407
What are you doing here? Why are you here?

01:07:18.906 --> 01:07:24.439
What exactly... is going on right now?

01:07:25.297 --> 01:07:30.473
I'm not entirely sure either,
but it seems like...

01:07:34.171 --> 01:07:37.497
something went wrong.

01:07:51.520 --> 01:07:55.271
[Do you want to go on a date with me?]

01:07:59.278 --> 01:08:02.389
[Failed to control my strength]

01:08:03.365 --> 01:08:06.618
[Is anger volatile or something?]

01:08:12.250 --> 01:08:15.970
[No. Don't go]

01:08:18.782 --> 01:08:21.179
According to the witnesses,

01:08:21.179 --> 01:08:24.075
there wasn't just one man.

01:08:24.075 --> 01:08:26.382
There were two.

01:08:26.382 --> 01:08:28.352
This is insane.

01:08:28.352 --> 01:08:30.829
I usually don't meddle
in other people's business,

01:08:30.829 --> 01:08:32.355
but when it comes to you, I keep stepping in.

01:08:32.355 --> 01:08:33.805
Something about this feels off.

01:08:33.805 --> 01:08:35.750
What do you think about the rumors?

01:08:35.750 --> 01:08:37.545
Wait, Ji Su?

01:08:37.545 --> 01:08:40.183
Is he actually close with Son Jeong A?

01:08:40.183 --> 01:08:42.176
Chance of rain, 46 percent.

01:08:42.176 --> 01:08:44.979
I've never seen anyone
prepare this much for a date.

01:08:44.979 --> 01:08:46.670
Do you even know what an opportunity is,

01:08:46.670 --> 01:08:48.594
you clueless guy?

01:08:48.594 --> 01:08:51.012
"Clueless?"
